WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
SpaceX completes the O3BM power constellation with a cape canaveral launch while preparing

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:13.720
a vandenberg mission for USS F-259. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 100. That's episode

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:20.080
100, a big milestone. Thank you for being here. The falcon 9 lifted off from Cape Canaveral

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.800
Space Force Station carrying the final three O3BM power satellites. This completes the constellation

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.680
build for SES. The launch marked an uncommon daytime departure from the Florida site. The falcon 9

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:40.400
second stage performed the required burns to reach the medium-earth orbit injection. The O3BM power

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.780
satellites represent a separate medium-earth orbit network distinct from Starlink's low-earth

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.260
orbit architecture. The higher altitude reduces the total number of satellites needed for coverage

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.160
while increasing the mass each launch must deliver. Multiple viewing opportunities were available

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:02.640
along Florida's Space Coast. Photos captured the rocket's streaking skyward after lift-off

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.000
from coastal vantage points. The launch marked an uncommon daytime departure from the Florida

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.780
site, rather than the more typical evening windows. Observers noted the sudden scheduling shift for

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:23.040
the O3BM power payload and Orlando Sentinel.com. The upcoming Falcon 9 mission from SLC4E at Vandenberg

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:31.180
SFB is scheduled for September 16th. Booster B1097 is slated for its 13th flight with landing

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:38.820
targeted on OCISLY. The mission will mark the 730th SpaceX launch overall if successful.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:49.340
The thread lists 669th Falcon family booster landing, 226th landing on OCISLY, and 214th consecutive

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:56.400
successful SpaceX launch if completed. Five-day turnaround at the pad and 27 days since the booster's

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.220
prior flight are tracked in the updates. UK disclosures confirm use of the Starshield network for

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.680
military communications. The contracts involve secure satellite services separate from commercial

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.120
Starlink operations. The announcements separate the military grade architecture from the public

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.720
constellation. Britain's Starshield disclosure lifts the curtain on SpaceX's quiet military

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.940
business through these UK filings. The disclosures confirm operational use by British forces.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.020
Contracts covered dedicated secure links distinct from the consumer constellation.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:38.800
Source add-hawk-news.de. Discussions point to potential direct-to-cell expansion into domestic

