development. SpaceX CFO Brett Johnson says China has an amazing space program, but it's not on a

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:57.440
Starship level. The statements were made in a finance interview setting. Global competition was

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:03.560
framed around payload capacity and reusability metrics. Viewers posted images of the Falcon 9

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.980
Ascent and Faring separation captured from coastal vantage points. The daytime timing

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:14.580
allowed clearer documentation than typical night launches. Multiple coastal locations provided

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.860
sightlines for the rare daytime Ascent. Florida observers share launch photos from the

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:26.340
O3BM power mission across social channels. The images show the full stack profile against daylight

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:33.540
skies. Faring separation was visible from several beaches. On the AI front no new source developments

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:40.680
appeared today on the SpaceX XAI GROC cursor compute thread. So the live threads to watch remain

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:48.880
orbital data centers direct to cell XAI compute and cursor GROC distribution. The engineering angle

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:55.400
here starts with the orbit altitude choice itself. Medium Earth orbit for the O3BM power satellites

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:01.060
demands that the Falcon 9 second stage carry extra propellant margin compared with low Earth orbit

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.560
missions, which directly limits the instantaneous launch window and forces a longer burn sequence

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:13.100
for precise insertion. That same altitude choice trades manufacturing volume for performance per

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.260
spacecraft. Since fewer total satellites are required yet each one must carry more

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:23.940
sophisticated phased array antennas and larger solar arrays sized for the greater distance to

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:29.620
ground users. The completed network therefore shows how orbit selection sets the minimum vehicle

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:37.280
performance floor for both the rocket and the satellite bus. In parallel the upcoming US SF-259

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:44.800
mission will reuse booster B1097 on its 13th flight, which compresses the operational cycle and

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.260
allows the vehicle to accumulate flight hours faster than expendable designs permit.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.640
The booster's entry and landing burns must again manage the thermal and structural loads

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:59.800
accumulated over prior missions, and the 27-day interval since the last flight further

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:06.060
validates the structural margins built into the octoweb and tank domes. The daytime Cape Canaveral

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:11.800
launch for the final O3B trio also shows how launch site weather and range constraints interact

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:17.160
with customer orbital requirements. Because a medium-earth orbit insertion requires extra

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:22.960
propellant margin that narrows the available windows. Together these elements form an interconnected

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:29.040
system where orbit selection, booster reuse cadence, and site-specific operations each

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:34.660
influence the achievable flight rate and per kilogram economics. Turning briefly to the markets,

